{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Slaughters, etc.</b> The sense: for I look to the one who trembles at My word, not to those who offer a burnt offering, and their deeds are evil. And so, one who slaughters an ox is as though he strikes a man — the meaning is, it is reckoned blood, for the burnt offering is not a proper offering. Or, it refers to one who strikes a man, not a fatal blow but a blow of wound and bruise." "<b>Who slaughters a lamb.</b> Before Me, it is as though he kills a dog." "And so <b>ערף</b> is a piel-pattern verb, and it means to cut the neck, and likewise וערפו there (Deuteronomy 21:4). And as it is there — [the text should read: it is a pausal form]." "<b>Who offers a meal offering.</b> As though he offers swine's blood." "<b>Who offers frankincense.</b> From the root of אזכרה (Leviticus 2:2); as though he blesses an idol." "And the sense of <b>they too</b> — the word 'your fathers' is to be supplied, and so it is: 'for your fathers, they too.'"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {2 "The bracketed correction צ״ל הנו מלעיל suggests the word should be understood as a pausal ( slowing) form; the manuscript reading הנה הנו appears defective."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:13.542805281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}